# MarketHub — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so it must
# never contain a real secret.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server data store
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the JSON store lives. Defaults to ./data/markethub.json.
# Point this at a mounted volume in a deployment so the file is not inside the
# deployed bundle. The directory `data/` is gitignored because the file holds
# scrypt password hashes and live session ids.
# MH_DATA_FILE=/var/lib/markethub/markethub.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Seeded demo accounts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Password given to every seeded sample account (the 8 sellers and 6 shoppers
# from src/lib/data.ts). Defaults to Demo@1234 when unset.
#
# This is only acceptable because every seeded account is fictional sample
# data. Do not reuse this value for anything real.
# MH_SEED_PASSWORD=Demo@1234

# The admin account is created ONLY if this is set, and there is no default.
# That is deliberate: a privileged account must never exist with a guessable
# password just because someone booted the app. Leave unset and no admin
# account is created at all.
# MH_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hubby AI assistant (pre-existing, optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without a key the assistant falls back to offline keyword matching.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to "production" in a deployment. This is what turns on the `Secure` flag
# on the session cookie, so leaving it unset over HTTPS would send the session
# cookie without Secure.
# NODE_ENV=production
